<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Minute is distributed outside the Mac App Store and does not use the App
    Sandbox, but release builds enable the hardened runtime. Under the
    hardened runtime the NSMicrophoneUsageDescription purpose string is not
    sufficient on its own: without the audio-input entitlement macOS denies
    microphone capture without ever showing the consent prompt, and the app
    never appears under Privacy & Security → Microphone (issue #1).

    Screen Recording has no hardened-runtime entitlement; its TCC prompt is
    governed by the purpose string alone.

    Production builds deliberately do not disable library validation. Tauri
    signs the app executable and bundled llama/ggml dylibs with the same
    Developer ID identity.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
